-- title:
--   Transfer of the cyclic-quotient j-reading between algebraic closures
-- statement:
--   Fix a commutative ring $A$, naturals $\ell_g, M', q$ with $M' \neq 0$, and three variable-change compatibilities, each quantified over all $A$-algebras $T$: $h_\ell$, that a $\Gamma_1$-point datum $D$ (a quadruple $x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q$ with $(x_P,y_P)$ on $W$, $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi\,\ell_g)(x_P)=0$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) transports along $C \bullet W$ to $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; $h_M$, that `IsGamma0PowAt` at $(p,k)$ transports to `kernelVariableChangeDeg` $C$ $(\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k)$ of the polynomial; and $h_L$, that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` transports correspondingly. Let $\mathcal G$ be a family of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A$-algebras, $\mathcal T$ a level transport of level $q$, and $R := \mathrm{rigidDataH1Pow}\,A\,\ell_g\,M'\,q\,h_\ell\,h_M\,h_L\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$ the resulting rigid Weierstrass datum. Let $K$ be a field over $A$ with $M' \neq 0$ in $K$, $x_0 \in R.\mathrm{Pt}\,K$, $y \in K$, and $d \neq 0$ with $d \mid M'$. Call a point $g$ of the affine curve of a raw datum cut out if $g$ has exact additive order $M'$ and, for every prime $p \mid M'$ and every $n$ such that $n \bullet g$ is an affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ of order $p^{v_p(M')}$, $x_1$ is a root of the $p$-th polynomial of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-slot `level.1` of the datum. Assume: for one algebraically closed field $\Omega_0$ over $K$ (compatibly over $A$) and one raw datum $x$ over $\Omega_0$ whose class in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\Omega_0$ is the image of $x_0$, every cut-out $g$ satisfies $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,\Omega_0\,y = \mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}$ of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ for the subgroup generated by $(M'/d) \bullet g$ and index datum $d$, that is, $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the corresponding cyclic quotient curve. Then for any further algebraically closed $\Omega$ over $K$, any raw datum $x'$ over $\Omega$ representing the image of $x_0$, and any cut-out point $g'$ on $x'.\mathrm{curve}$, one has $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,\Omega\,y = \mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\,(x'.\mathrm{curve})\,(\mathrm{zmultiples}\,((M'/d) \bullet g'))\,d$.
--
--   This is the well-definedness (base-change invariance) statement for reading the $j$-invariant of a cyclic quotient off a $K$-rational point of the $H_1$-type moduli datum: the value is independent of the algebraically closed field over $K$, of the chosen raw representative and of the chosen cut-out generator of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-cyclic subgroup. It is used in the Tate-curve computation attached to $\Gamma_1$-pinned points, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.algebraMap_jqNModC_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_of_eq_map_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.algebraMap_jqNModC_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_of_eq_map_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1).
